{
  "case": "ratko_mladic",
  "case_id_base": "IT-09-92",
  "case_id_transcript": "IT-09-92",
  "date": "2014-09-19",
  "utterances": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "speaker": "JUDGE ORIE",
      "role": "judge",
      "is_accused": false,
      "type": "statement",
      "text": "Good morning to everyone in and around this courtroom. Madam Registrar, would you please call the case."
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "speaker": "THE REGISTRAR",
      "role": "registrar",
      "is_accused": false,
      "type": "statement",
      "text": "Good morning, Your Honours. This is case IT-09-92-T, the Prosecutor versus Ratko Mladic."
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "speaker": "JUDGE ORIE",
      "role": "judge",
      "is_accused": false,
      "type": "statement",
      "text": "Thank you, Madam Registrar. Before we resume the examination of the witness I would like to briefly deal with a few matters. First of all, and surprisingly that it's already done which is highly appreciated by the Chamber, I inform the parties that the verification of the transcript of yesterday has been done and I -- this will be filed so the parties will see all that. There are a few corrections to the translation which we received yesterday, the interpretation, but on the most important sentence which was translated to us as \"but probably with the aim of either destroying the enemy or someone else who was positioned there,\" that part has been slightly corrected and the verified interpretation now is \"but probably with the aim of destroying the enemy or someone who was operating there.\" As you may remember, the issue whether it was \"someone who\" or \"something that.\" It's now \"someone who was operating there,\" which contradicts the further explanation of the witness. That's one. I'll put it to the witness once he has entered the courtroom. I have a few other matters, mainly related to translations. First, about P6708. On the 28th of August, 2014, during the testimony of Velimir Dunjic, the Prosecution was asked to upload P6708 and the document was marked for identification in order to allow the Defence to compare the original with the translation. The same day, P6708 was uploaded into e-court. Yesterday, the 18th of September, the Defence informed the Chamber through informal communication that it agreed with the translation. P6708 is therefore admitted into evidence. I now deal with translations for Exhibits D591 up to and including D593. On the 23rd of July, Exhibits D591, D592, and D593 were marked for identification pending translation. On the 17th of September, the Defence informed the Chamber, again through informal communication, that the translations have been uploaded into e-court under doc ID 1D09-3706 for D591, doc ID 1D09-3687 for D592, and doc ID 1D09-3707 for D593. And subject to the Prosecution's agreement asked the Chamber to connect the translation with the according originals. The same day, the Prosecution informed the Chamber again through an informal communication that it did not object the translations. Madam Registrar, you are instructed to connect the said translation with the according exhibits. Once that's done, D591 and D593 are admitted into evidence, and the Chamber would like to know from the Defence -- from the Prosecution whether they still object the admission of D592."
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "speaker": "MS. BIBLES",
      "role": "counsel",
      "is_accused": false,
      "type": "statement",
      "text": "We'll advise the Chamber after the next break, Your Honour."
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "speaker": "JUDGE ORIE",
      "role": "judge",
      "is_accused": false,
      "type": "statement",
      "text": "We'll hear from you and then we may decide on D592. We will continue the examination of the witness in private session, but for the witness to enter the courtroom, we first have to move into closed session."
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "speaker": "JUDGE ORIE",
